# Design Polish — Incremental Only

Use the **Hallmark** skill (`hallmark`) for visual/UX quality when building or refining marketing UI. Prefer small, targeted improvements over greenfield redesigns.

If `design.md` exists at the project root, it overrides Hallmark's default theme rotation for this repo.

## Brand visual anchors (existing)

- Tokens in `src/app/globals.css`: `mainColor`, `secondaryColor`, `thirdColor`, `otherColor`, light/dark surfaces
- Layout utilities: `margin`, `spacing`, `left-padding` / `right-padding`
- Established section rhythm on home, services, Insight, portfolio — preserve unless redesign is requested

## Default mode for this repo

- **Polish in place** — hierarchy, spacing, contrast, motion restraint, empty states
- **Keep the shell** — navbar, footer, bottom nav, existing section components, shadcn/ui
- **Do not** swap the whole marketing look (new theme catalog, global font/color overhaul) unless the user asks for a redesign or `hallmark redesign`

## When Hallmark is appropriate

- New marketing sections that must match GONLINE's current language
- `hallmark audit <target>` — ranked punch list only, no edits
- Scoped polish (cards, CTAs, Insight list, forms) called out by the user

## Hard stops

- Do not delete route trees or rewrite `src/components/ui/`
- Do not replace established patterns (SmartImage, section spacing, Insight cards) with a new design system
- If a “redesign” would touch many unrelated files, stop and confirm scope first

## Stack constraints

Next.js App Router · shadcn/ui · Tailwind v4 · Tailwind-first styling · honest brand copy
